@@ -0,0 +1,291 @@
+# Signed URLs for the download host — install & migration guide
+
+**Version:** bridge `1.8.0` · **Schema:** unchanged (`1.7.0`) · **Host:** `dll.mrdastbaaf.com`
+**Replaces:** `docs/DLL_HOST_HTACCESS.sample` (Referer-based hotlink protection)
+
+---
+
+## The problem this solves
+
+Until now `POST /lessons/{id}/playback` returned a **permanent, unsigned** URL:
+
+```
+https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4
+```
+
+Anyone who saw that URL once — in the Network tab, in a proxy log, in a
+screenshot — could download the video forever, with no login and no
+subscription. The only defence was Referer-based hotlink protection, and a
+Referer header is trivially forged:
+
+```bash
+curl -e "https://app.mrdastbaaf.com/" https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4   # 200 OK
+```
+
+The `.htaccess` layer stops casual link-sharing. It stops nothing else.
+
+## What changes
+
+The server now appends a short-lived signature to every video URL:
+
+```
+https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4?md5=<sig>&expires=1800000000
+```
+
+nginx validates it **before** serving a single byte. A URL without a valid
+signature is `403`; an expired one is `410`.
+
+This is `ngx_http_secure_link_module`, which nginx ships natively — no extra
+software, no CDN dependency, and it works on the existing shared host.
+
+### The algorithm
+
+Both sides must compute this identically:
+
+```
+signature = base64url( md5( expires . uri . secret , raw ) )
+```
+
+where `base64url` means `+`→`-`, `/`→`_`, and no `=` padding.
+
+nginx:
+
+```nginx
+secure_link      $arg_md5,$arg_expires;
+secure_link_md5  "$secure_link_expires$uri$secret";
+```
+
+PHP (`MrDastbaaf_Signed_Url_Service::sign()`):
+
+```php
+$raw = md5($expires . $resource . $secret, true);
+$sig = rtrim(strtr(base64_encode($raw), '+/', '-_'), '=');
+```
+
+A fixed vector is locked down by `tests/php/test-signed-urls.php` and
+independently cross-checked against a separate implementation:
+
+| Input | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `resource` | `/FA/lesson-01.mp4` |
+| `expires` | `1800000000` |
+| `secret` | `test-secret` |
+| **signature** | `uydm921XT5rHRgrrCIVrgA` |
+
+If that test ever fails, **stop** — a mismatch means every video on the platform
+returns 403.
+
+### Two traps, both handled
+
+**1. `$uri` in nginx is percent-decoded.** This project's filenames are Persian,
+so they arrive as `/FA/%D8%AF%D8%B1%D8%B3.mp4`. nginx sees the *decoded* path
+while PHP reads the raw one. Signing the encoded form would make every signature
+invalid — silently, and only in production, and only for non-ASCII filenames.
+`path_for_signing()` decodes, and the signed URL keeps the original encoded path.
+The test suite asserts that the encoded and decoded forms produce different
+signatures, so the distinction cannot be lost by accident.
+
+**2. The signature is not bound to the client IP.** Binding it would make sharing
+harder, but a phone switching from 4G to Wi-Fi mid-playback changes IP and would
+get a 403 in the middle of a lesson. The IP-bound variant is present but commented
+in the sample config.
+
+---
+
+## Rollout — follow this order
+
+> ⚠️ **If nginx enforces the signature before PHP sends it, every video 403s.**
+> The order below makes that impossible: PHP starts signing while nginx is still
+> permissive, so you can verify the happy path before you close the door.
+
+### Step 1 — confirm the module exists
+
+```bash
+nginx -V 2>&1 | tr ' ' '\n' | grep secure_link
+```
+
+Empty output means `nginx-light` or a build without the module. Install
+`nginx-full` or the nginx.org package first — do not continue.
+
+### Step 2 — agree on the secret
+
+Generate one long random value and put it **in both places**.
+
+In `wp-config.php` (recommended — one source of truth, never in a DB dump):
+
+```php
+define('MRDASTBAAF_SIGNED_URL_SECRET', 'a-long-random-value-you-generate');
+```
+
+If you skip this, the plugin generates one and stores it in the option
+`mrdastbaaf_signed_url_secret`; read it with
+`wp option get mrdastbaaf_signed_url_secret`.
+
+Then set the same value in the nginx `map` block.
+
+**A mismatch means every request 403s.** Verify character-for-character.
+
+### Step 3 — install the nginx config in permissive mode
+
+Copy `docs/DLL_HOST_NGINX_SIGNED_URLS.sample` into your server block, and leave
+these two lines **commented out**:
+
+```nginx
+# if ($secure_link = "") { return 403; }
+# if ($secure_link = "0") { return 410; }
+```
+
+```bash
+nginx -t && nginx -s reload
+```
+
+Nothing is blocked yet. Playback should be entirely unaffected.
+
+### Step 4 — turn on signing in PHP
+
+```php
+update_option('mrdastbaaf_signed_urls_enabled', true);
+```
+
+Or filter it in, if you prefer config over database:
+
+```php
+add_filter('mrdastbaaf_signed_urls_enabled', '__return_true');
+```
+
+Now `POST /lessons/{id}/playback` returns URLs carrying `?md5=…&expires=…`, and
+the response also carries `"signedUrls": true`.
+
+**Verify playback works in the web PWA and in the app.** The URLs are signed but
+nginx is not checking them yet, so the only thing that can break here is PHP —
+and if it does, you have not closed anything off yet.
+
+### Step 5 — confirm unsigned access is still open
+
+```bash
+curl -I "https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4"     # expect 200
+```
+
+If this is already 403, something else is blocking (the old `.htaccess` is still
+in place — see step 7).
+
+### Step 6 — enforce
+
+Uncomment the two `if` lines and reload:
+
+```bash
+nginx -t && nginx -s reload
+```
+
+Now verify, in this order:
+
+```bash
+# 1. No signature → 403
+curl -I "https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4"
+
+# 2. Valid signature → 200, with "Accept-Ranges: bytes"
+curl -I "https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4?md5=<sig>&expires=<future>"
+
+# 3. Tampered signature → 403
+curl -I "https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4?md5=AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA&expires=<future>"
+
+# 4. Expired signature → 410
+curl -I "https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4?md5=<sig>&expires=1000000000"
+
+# 5. Range request (seeking) → 206 Partial Content
+curl -I -H "Range: bytes=0-1023" "https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4?md5=<sig>&expires=<future>"
+```
+
+Build the signature for tests 2 and 5 with:
+
+```bash
+php -r 'echo rtrim(strtr(base64_encode(md5((time()+3600)."/FA/lesson-01.mp4"."YOUR_SECRET", true)), "+/", "-_"), "=");'
+```
+
+Then **play a full lesson in the app, seek around, and let it run past the TTL**
+(default 15 minutes) to confirm playback does not stall mid-video.
+
+### Step 7 — remove the old Referer-based protection
+
+Once step 6 passes, delete the `.htaccess` from the `dll.` host root (or remove
+its `SetEnvIf`/`RewriteRule` blocks).
+
+Keeping it causes confusing double-failures: a signed request can still be
+rejected by the Referer rules, and you will be debugging the wrong layer. The
+signed URL is strictly stronger and makes the hotlink layer redundant.
+
+### Step 8 — turn the PHP stream proxy OFF
+
+The stream proxy (`mrdastbaaf_stream_proxy_mode`) existed to hide the CDN URL
+behind a 60-second token. Signed URLs achieve the same goal properly, without
+proxying every byte through PHP.
+
+Turn it off:
+
+```php
+update_option('mrdastbaaf_stream_proxy_mode', false);
+```
+
+The proxy also had two defects that signed URLs do not have: its token was never
+bound to the requesting user, and it expired 60 seconds into a video, killing
+playback mid-lesson.
+
+---
+
+## Rollback
+
+Any step reverses cleanly:
+
+| To undo | Do |
+|---|---|
+| Enforcement | comment the two `if` lines, `nginx -s reload` |
+| Signing | `update_option('mrdastbaaf_signed_urls_enabled', false)` |
+| Everything | restore the previous nginx config and re-enable the proxy |
+
+Rolling back enforcement alone is enough to restore service: with the `if` lines
+commented, both signed and unsigned URLs work again.
+
+---
+
+## What this does and does not achieve
+
+**Does:** makes a leaked URL worthless within minutes. A URL captured from a
+network log, a shared screenshot, or a Telegram group stops working. Combined
+with the 30-day ticket flow, obtaining a *usable* URL now requires an active
+subscription at the moment of the request.
+
+**Does not:** stop a determined attacker. Someone with a valid subscription can
+still play the video and capture it — screen-record it, or re-request a fresh
+signed URL through their own authenticated client. No URL-signing scheme prevents
+that; only DRM would, and DRM is out of scope for this project.
+
+It also does not stop re-recording, which is what the dynamic watermark is for:
+the watermark identifies *who* leaked a recording, the signature limits *how
+long* a leaked URL is useful.
+
+The honest summary: this closes the "one leaked URL is a permanent public
+download" hole, which was the largest practical gap. It does not make the content
+uncopyable, and nothing at this layer can.
+
+---
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+| Symptom | Likely cause |
+|---|---|
+| **Everything** 403s | Secret mismatch between PHP and nginx, or signing enabled in nginx before PHP |
+| Only **Persian-named** files 403 | The `$uri` decode trap — confirm `path_for_signing()` is in use and the test suite passes |
+| 403 on files **outside `/FA/`** | The `location` does not cover them; add a `location` block or move the files |
+| 200 with no signature | The `if` lines are still commented (step 6 not done) |
+| 200 but no `Accept-Ranges` | Range support was disabled; check `sendfile`/`aio` settings |
+| Playback dies after ~15 min | TTL too short for the lesson; raise `mrdastbaaf_signed_url_ttl` (max 86 400) |
+| Works in the browser, fails in the app | A proxy/WAF stripping the query string — check what reaches the origin |
+
+## Configuration reference
+
+| Option | Default | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `mrdastbaaf_signed_urls_enabled` | `false` | Off by default so the rollout order above is the only way to enable it |
+| `mrdastbaaf_signed_url_ttl` | `900` (15 min) | Clamped to `[1, 86400]` |
+| `mrdastbaaf_signed_url_secret` | auto-generated | Overridden by the `MRDASTBAAF_SIGNED_URL_SECRET` constant |
+| Filter `mrdastbaaf_signed_urls_enabled` | — | Force on/off without touching the database |
